/**
 * Compliance cluster — the Texas structural pest control licence explained.
 *
 * The E-E-A-T anchor of the compliance tree, and the page that makes the
 * published licence number mean something.
 *
 * Verified Aug 2026 against 4 TAC ch. 7 subchapter H (Structural Pest Control
 * Service), retrieved via Cornell LII and Justia mirrors:
 *  - §7.121 Types and Requirements of Licenses — seven classes, (a) business
 *    licensee through (g) apprentice. A business licence is required for each
 *    business LOCATION and must name a responsible certified commercial
 *    applicator who does not hold that role anywhere else. The business licence
 *    reflects only categories in which an active certified applicator is
 *    employed, and requires the responsible applicator AND current general
 *    liability insurance to be maintained at all times.
 *  - §7.123 Insurance Requirements.
 *  - §7.124 Structural License Categories — SEVEN official categories. The
 *    official name of the termite category is "Termite and Wood Destroying
 *    Insect Control", not "Termite".
 *  - §7.126 Licensing Qualification Requirements — category exam + general
 *    standards exam, plus 12 of the past 24 months supervised experience with
 *    at least 6 months holding a technician licence, or an accredited
 *    biological-sciences degree/certificate, or prior/out-of-state equivalents.
 *  - §7.127 License Expiration and Renewal (annual).
 *  - §7.132 Apprentice — min age 16, 20 classroom hours general standards
 *    (2 hours in each of 10 subjects), plus 40 hours OJT and 8 classroom hours
 *    per category, max 12 months, technician exam pass mark 70%.
 *  - §7.133 Technician — 8 classroom + 40 OJT hours to add a category; 8 hours
 *    verifiable training per year to renew, max 2 of which may be OJT.
 *  - §7.134 Continuing Education — TWO general CEUs plus ONE per held category,
 *    per CALENDAR year, at annual renewal. At least one general unit must cover
 *    laws, pesticide safety, environmental protection or IPM. No course repeats
 *    for credit within a calendar year. Self-study only every other year, never
 *    two years running. Certificates kept two calendar years.
 *
 * HONESTY GATES:
 *  - RESOLVED 31 August 2026, against the certificate itself. TPCL 0976265 is
 *    the TDA TPCL number; 0946390 is the separate applicator "License No" and
 *    is deliberately NOT published — see business.ts. The page still explains
 *    that both kinds of number exist and still tells the reader to check ours
 *    against TDA records, which was always the point and is now also testable.
 *  - Do NOT state a CEU figure for this business as fact beyond what the rule
 *    arithmetic gives (2 general + 1 per category held).
 *  - AgriLife's gloss that "only one CEU annually may come from self-study" is
 *    an imprecise restatement of §7.134(e). Follow the rule text.
 */
